# Personal Codebase Memory MCP excludes (local only: listed in .git/info/exclude).
# Goal: index the code and docs that matter for cross-repo links, not data.

# JSON and other data files become thousands of Variable nodes and bury code.
*.json
*.jsonl
*.csv
*.sql

# Build output, caches, and generated assets.
dist/
build/
target/
out/
coverage/
.next/
*.min.js
*.map
logs/
temp/
tmp/

# Forks in lib/. Nibiru is moving the parts it relies on into modules it
# owns, so the code it builds on stays indexed (Unique, 2026-11-17):
#   kept: lib/cosmos-sdk, lib/cosmwasm-vm, the public surface of lib/wasmvm
#   (wvm/ and top-level Go files), lib/nibiru-std, lib/nibiru-ownable-derive.
# Excluded: forks Nibiru doesn't change much, and test or generated code
# that would crowd search results.
/lib/wasmer/
/lib/ibc-go/
/lib/cosmwasm-optimizer/
/lib/wasmvm/internal/
/lib/wasmvm/libwasmvm/
/lib/wasmvm/builders/
/lib/cosmos-sdk/contrib/
/lib/cosmos-sdk/docs/
/lib/cosmos-sdk/**/testutil/
/lib/cosmos-sdk/**/*.pb.go
/lib/**/simulation/
/lib/**/*_test.go
# CometBFT fork (consensus engine), not needed for app-level questions.
/bft/
# Compiled contract artifacts and generated REST gateways.
/evm/embeds/artifacts/
*.pb.gw.go
# Registries and reports that are data, not code.
/token-registry/
/security-reports/
